-- title:
--   Measurability of $u\mapsto W_{2,T}(\mu_u,\nu_u)$ for measurable law families
-- statement:
--   Let $C_d=C([0,T];\mathbb R^d)$ be the space of continuous paths on the horizon $[0,T]$ with the uniform norm $\|x\|_{*,T}=\sup_{0\le s\le T}|x(s)|$, equipped with its Borel $\sigma$-field, and let $\mathcal P(C_d)$ carry the Giry $\sigma$-field (generated by the evaluations $\mu\mapsto\mu(A)$). For probability measures $\mu,\nu$ on $C_d$ write
--
--   $$W_{2,T}(\mu,\nu)=\Bigl(\inf_{\pi\in\Pi(\mu,\nu)}\int\|x-y\|_{*,T}^2\,\pi(dx,dy)\Bigr)^{1/2}\in[0,\infty],$$
--
--   the infimum running over couplings $\pi$ of $\mu$ and $\nu$.
--
--   Let $(A,\mathcal A)$ be any measurable space and let $a\mapsto\mu_a$ and $a\mapsto\nu_a$ be measurable maps from $A$ into the probability measures on $C_d$. Then the map
--
--   $$A\ni a\longmapsto W_{2,T}(\mu_a,\nu_a)\in[0,\infty]$$
--
--   is measurable.
--
--   In Bayraktar–Chakraborty–Wu this is what makes the integrated distances $\int_I[W_{2,t}(\mu^{G_n}_u,\mu^G_u)]^2\,du$ in Theorem 2.1(c) well defined, the label-wise laws $u\mapsto\mu^{G}_u$ being measurable by Proposition 2.1 and Remark 5.1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $W_{2,T}$ is `W2T`, the published coupling definition `wassersteinDistance 2` on `Cd T d`; it takes values in `ENNReal`. Measurability of the families is with respect to Mathlib's Giry $\sigma$-algebra on `Measure (Cd T d)`.
-- source:
--   Bayraktar, Chakraborty, Wu, Graphon mean field systems, Ann. Appl. Probab. 33(5) (2023), arXiv:2003.13180; p. 3604 (proof of Theorem 2.1(c): 'Using Remark 5.1, the left hand side below is well-defined') and p. 3601, Remark 5.1; lower semicontinuity of W_2 under weak convergence: Villani, Optimal Transport: Old and New (2009), Remark 6.12; Giry sigma-field = Borel sigma-field of the weak topology on P(X) for Polish X: Kechris, Classical Descriptive Set Theory, Theorem 17.24.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GraphonMF_Stability_Setting

open MeasureTheory
open scoped ENNReal NNReal

namespace GraphonMF.Stability

/-- Measurability of the label-wise path-space Wasserstein distance, used (via Remark 5.1,
p. 3601) to make the left-hand side of (5.6) on p. 3604 well defined. -/
theorem measurable_W2T {α : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α] {T : ℝ≥0} {d : ℕ}
    (μ ν : α → Measure (Cd T d)) (hμ : Measurable μ) (hν : Measurable ν)
    (hμp : ∀ a, IsProbabilityMeasure (μ a)) (hνp : ∀ a, IsProbabilityMeasure (ν a)) :
    Measurable (fun a => W2T (μ a) (ν a)) := by sorry

end GraphonMF.Stability
